      "writtenOn": "2024-05-29T16:33:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I really do think that you should modify the RFCOMM interface to have something meaningful to assert on, like a status (for example https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/pandora/bt-test-interfaces/pandora/a2dp.proto;l\u003d130-138;drc\u003dab8427a340e282875745a8a69e19ad38b4dd233e) or for example if the RFCOMM channel is considered secure or insecure.\n\nHere we are still asserting an id that has nothing to do with the DUT nor RFCOMM.\n\nIf needed, I can help updating the PandoraServer and pts-bot to account for the modifications of the RFCOMM interface (Or we can also create a new RFCOMM interface, like RFCOMM2 if we don\u0027t want to the update now).\n\nConsider this comment as a nitpick, if you don\u0027t have the time to work on this, I\u0027m also fine to remove the assert and create a bug to track that.",
